    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using blast chillers can indeed change the documentation required for your HACCP audit. Blast chillers are considered a \"rapid cooling\" method, which means that the cooling process is faster than traditional air cooling or ice baths.\n\nIn this case, you'll need to document the specific temperature and time parameters for the blast chiller, as well as the equipment's specifications and calibration records. This is because the blast chiller's performance can affect the cooling rate and consistency, which in turn can impact the safety of the final product.\n\nTypically, you'll need to document the following:\n\n* Blast chiller temperature and time parameters\n* Equipment specifications, including temperature range and cooling rate\n* Calibration records for the blast chiller\n* Monitoring and control procedures for the blast chiller\n* Records of any adjustments or maintenance performed on the blast chiller\n\nIt's essential to ensure that your documentation is accurate, complete, and up-to-date to demonstrate compliance with regulatory requirements and industry standards. A thorough review of your HACCP plan and documentation will help you identify any potential areas for improvement and ensure that your logs will pass inspection.",
